  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_rating",
      "components": ["T2", "D5", "D6", "R49"],
      "pins": ["T2.1", "T2.2", "D5.1", "D6.1", "D6.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0061", "/+24V_{F}", "GND"],
      "observed": "T2 is an AON6407 P-channel MOSFET with its source on /+24V_{F} and gate on /NET0061. D6 is a 12 V zener from the gate net to GND, while R49 connects the gate to the source net. D5 is a 28 V TVS from /+24V_{F} to GND with a specified 45.4 V clamp. At that clamp voltage, D6 limits the gate to about 12 V, exposing T2 to roughly 33 V of |VGS|, above the MOSFET's ±20 V absolute maximum.",
      "expected": "The gate-source voltage should remain within T2's ±20 V rating over the protected input range, including the TVS clamp condition; use a source-referenced gate clamp or otherwise limit the differential voltage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/+24V_{F}\") ... (node (ref \"T2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\")) ... (node (ref \"D5\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/NET0061\") ... (node (ref \"D6\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\")) ... (node (ref \"R49\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"T2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"D5\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")) (node (ref \"D6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"D5\") (value \"28V\") ... (description \"TVS Diode 28VWM 45.4V Clamp 13.2A Ipp Tvs Diode Surface Mount SMB\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"T2\") (value \"AON6407\") ... (description \"P-Channel 30 V 32A ...\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "During a sufficiently large input transient, the TVS can clamp the source rail well above the gate's ground-referenced zener voltage. The resulting excessive gate-source voltage can damage T2 and compromise the board's input protection.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The gate clamp for the 24 V input P-channel MOSFET is referenced to ground rather than its source. At the documented TVS clamp voltage, the resulting gate-source differential can exceed T2's absolute maximum rating."
}

